{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And therefore YHWH waits.</b> In the manner of human speech:" "<b>To show you grace.</b> Of the doubled-[letter] verbs, on the pattern of אין גחלת לחמם (Isaiah 47:14), from the light binyan, on the pattern of לשכב את בת יעקב. And if they are anomalous in grammar:" "<b>And therefore</b> He will rise to show you compassion, for HaShem will do justice for you against Assyria:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {1 "The phrase 'ואם הם זרות בדקדוק' is opaque; translated hyper-literally. The referent of 'they' and the precise force of זרות ('foreign/anomalous') is ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:02.557451223Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}